WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.267 --> 00:00:03.369
-The president is facing
an independent challenge

00:00:03.369 --> 00:00:05.471
from the former C.E.O.
of Starbucks

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:07.473
and a tell-all book
from a former aide.

00:00:07.473 --> 00:00:09.976
For more on this, it's time for
"A Closer Look."

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:13.846
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:16.549
President Trump's approval
ratings are record lows,

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.751
and there are already
several prominent Democrats

00:00:18.751 --> 00:00:21.153
with serious track records
lining up to run against him.

00:00:21.153 --> 00:00:23.156
And then,
there's Howard Schultz,

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:25.625
the billionaire former C.E.O.
of Starbucks.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:27.693
Schultz has been
attacking Democrats,

00:00:27.693 --> 00:00:29.929
and says he wants to run
a centrist, independent

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.130
campaign for president.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:33.799
And so far, the rollout
has been a disaster.

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:35.969
-Former Starbucks C.E.O.
Howard Schultz

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.637
got an earful
from a protester

00:00:37.637 --> 00:00:39.838
at a New York City
book signing Monday night,

00:00:39.838 --> 00:00:41.975
after Schultz said
he is seriously considering

00:00:41.975 --> 00:00:44.143
a possible Independent run
for the White House --

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:47.647
a move that many Democrats fear
could split the anti-Trump vote

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.415
and help re-elect
the president.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:53.019
-I am seriously considering
running for president

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:55.488
as a centrist
Independent.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:57.790
And I wanted to clarify
the word "Independent,"

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:03.129
which I view merely as
a designation on the ballot.

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.532
-Don't help elect Trump,

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:10.103
you egotistical
billionaire [bleep]!

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:11.571
-Damn.

00:01:11.571 --> 00:01:15.975
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.975 --> 00:01:20.879
It is not good
when people are yelling at you

00:01:20.879 --> 00:01:23.650
at your first
campaign event.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.018
He's like a stand-up comedian
who gets heckled

00:01:26.018 --> 00:01:28.821
before he's even
told a joke.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:29.923
"How's everybody
doing tonight?"

00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.525
"You suck!"

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:34.193
By the way,
that event was at

00:01:34.193 --> 00:01:35.728
the Barnes and Noble
in Union Square,

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.430
which has a Starbucks
in it.

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:40.800
He got heckled
in one of his own stores.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:42.802
That's like if the Colonel
showed up at KFC

00:01:42.802 --> 00:01:44.604
and got his head dunked
in the fryer.

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.405
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:50.709
There is virtually no appetite
for a billionaire businessman

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.545
to run for president
right now.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:55.448
I guess somebody really put
a stink on that genre.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:56.649
[ Laughter ]

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:58.885
Running as a billionaire now
is like saying,

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:02.321
"We should do a music festival
with Ja Rule on an island."

00:02:02.321 --> 00:02:05.358
[ Laughter, cheers ]

00:02:08.227 --> 00:02:10.830
And instead of making a case
for why he should be president,

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:13.565
Schultz has been going after
Democrats like Elizabeth Warren,

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:15.068
Kamala Harris,
Bernie Sanders,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.070
and even
Alexandria Ocasio-Cortez.

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:19.138
-In order to run
as a Democrat today,

00:02:19.138 --> 00:02:22.876
you have to fall in line with
free Medicare for everybody --

00:02:22.876 --> 00:02:25.145
free --
free college for everybody.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.647
I don't think
their views represent

00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:30.182
the majority
of Americans.

00:02:30.182 --> 00:02:33.986
I don't think we want
a 70% income tax in America.

00:02:33.986 --> 00:02:37.757
When I see Elizabeth Warren
come out with, you know,

00:02:37.757 --> 00:02:44.330
a ridiculous plan of taxing
wealthy people a surtax of 2%

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.934
because it makes a good
headline, or sends out a tweet,

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:50.002
when she knows for a fact
that's not something

00:02:50.002 --> 00:02:53.206
that's ever gonna be passed --
this is what's wrong.

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:54.573
You just played --

00:02:54.573 --> 00:02:57.910
Senator Harris is saying
she wants to abolish

00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.612
the insurance industry.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.980
That's --
That's not correct.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.416
That's not American.
What's next?

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.451
What industry are we
going to abolish next?

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:06.986
The coffee industry?

00:03:06.986 --> 00:03:08.388
-No, dude.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.788
There's a difference,
for one thing.

00:03:09.788 --> 00:03:11.891
You can make coffee
at home.

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.359
But every time I try to
home-brew some insulin,

00:03:14.359 --> 00:03:16.162
my lab rat has a seizure.

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.763
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.763 --> 00:03:22.234
Seriously, you think people
are gonna vote for you?

00:03:22.234 --> 00:03:25.003
You over them, because you're
the C.E.O. of a coffee company?

00:03:25.003 --> 00:03:27.373
Personally, I'm more of
a Dunkin' Donuts guy,

00:03:27.373 --> 00:03:29.742
but that doesn't mean
I'm gonna vote for the C.E.O. --

00:03:29.742 --> 00:03:32.612
who I assume is just
a drunk guy in a Bruins jersey

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:34.646
chucking snowballs
off a highway overpass.

00:03:34.646 --> 00:03:36.683
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:41.621
"Check out our
cro-sandwiches!"

00:03:41.621 --> 00:03:43.389
[ Laughter ]

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.825
If Schultz really doesn't like
the current Democratic field,

00:03:45.825 --> 00:03:48.494
he could just run against them
in a Democratic primary.

00:03:48.494 --> 00:03:50.596
But he wants to bypass
the process

00:03:50.596 --> 00:03:52.598
because he thinks
he's entitled to it.

00:03:52.598 --> 00:03:55.000
That's right --
the guy who ran Starbucks

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:58.037
doesn't want
to wait in line.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.739
But Schultz doesn't even
seem to know

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:01.474
the basic facts
about how elections work.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.975
In an interview on
"60 Minutes," for example,

00:04:02.975 --> 00:04:05.111
he pledged to get on the ballot
in all 50 states.

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.680
But then, he said something
that made no sense.

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.149
-If I decide to run
for president,

00:04:10.149 --> 00:04:12.585
not only will I be on the ballot
of every state --

00:04:12.585 --> 00:04:14.019
all 50 states --

00:04:14.019 --> 00:04:17.056
but will be on the ballot in
every county and every district.

00:04:17.056 --> 00:04:18.157
-What?

00:04:18.157 --> 00:04:20.125
If you're on the ballot
in the state,

00:04:20.125 --> 00:04:21.294
you're on the ballot

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:23.997
in every county and district
in that state.

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:26.499
Every county and every district
isn't a presidential plan.

00:04:26.499 --> 00:04:29.235
It's a Starbucks
expansion plan.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.570
And we don't want a president
who can't separate

00:04:31.570 --> 00:04:33.306
his last job
from his current job.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:34.640
This guy was a builder.

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.942
Now, all he does is talk about
building a wall.

00:04:36.942 --> 00:04:38.811
Instead of healthcare,
what are you gonna give us?

00:04:38.811 --> 00:04:39.979
Cake pops?

00:04:39.979 --> 00:04:41.247
[ Laughter ]

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:43.649
So, Schultz's initial rollout
has not gone well,

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:45.751
which meant Trump couldn't help
but comment on it.

00:04:45.751 --> 00:04:47.620
Because when Trump sees someone
getting attention

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:49.121
for doing something dumb,
he gets jealous,

00:04:49.121 --> 00:04:50.856
and does something dumber.

00:04:50.856 --> 00:04:53.292
And earlier this week,
he attacked Schultz in a tweet.

00:04:53.292 --> 00:04:56.328
-"Howard Schultz doesn't have
the guts to run for president.

00:04:56.328 --> 00:04:58.163
Watched him on '60 Minutes'
last night,

00:04:58.163 --> 00:05:00.900
and I agree with him that
he's not the smartest person.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.702
Besides,
America already has that.

00:05:03.702 --> 00:05:06.706
I only hope that Starbucks
is still paying me their rent

00:05:06.706 --> 00:05:08.007
in Trump Tower."

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:11.978
-Okay, first of all --
why would anyone in New York

00:05:11.978 --> 00:05:13.546
go to the Starbucks
in Trump Tower?

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:15.948
There's two
on every block.

00:05:15.948 --> 00:05:19.652
That's like going to a Mets game
just for the Shake Shack.

00:05:19.652 --> 00:05:20.853
The food might be good,

00:05:20.853 --> 00:05:23.923
but you've still got to
watch the Mets.

00:05:23.923 --> 00:05:25.057
Second,
Trump just admitted

00:05:25.057 --> 00:05:26.793
he still makes money
from his businesses.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:30.263
You're supposed to lie, and say
your business is separate.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:32.798
If Vladimir Putin announced that
he was running for president,

00:05:32.798 --> 00:05:35.434
Trump would tweet, "I hope
he's still paying me bribes."

00:05:35.434 --> 00:05:36.768
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.768 --> 00:05:39.772
When Trump sees a grift,
he can't help but get in on it,

00:05:39.772 --> 00:05:41.273
because he's
a life-long grifter.

00:05:41.273 --> 00:05:43.709
And the thing about grifters is,
they attract other grifters.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:45.344
That's why Trump's campaign
and White House

00:05:45.344 --> 00:05:46.578
are filled with
scam artists.

00:05:46.578 --> 00:05:48.780
His personal lawyer set up
a secret slush fund

00:05:48.780 --> 00:05:49.915
to take bribes,

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.584
his first
National Security Adviser

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:53.619
was lobbying for a foreign
government on the side,

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:56.889
and his acting Attorney General
had a scam company

00:05:56.889 --> 00:05:58.858
that helped sell
hot tubs.

00:05:58.858 --> 00:06:00.526
I'm pretty sure
that's how Trump found him.

00:06:00.526 --> 00:06:02.161
[ As Trump ] "Hello.
I'd like to order a hot tub.

00:06:02.161 --> 00:06:05.164
Also, by any chance,
are you a lawyer?"

00:06:05.164 --> 00:06:06.565
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:07.633
[ Normal voice ] You've got
all these grifters

00:06:07.633 --> 00:06:08.834
surrounding
the president.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:10.736
And even when they leave,
the grift doesn't end.

00:06:10.736 --> 00:06:12.772
That's when they try
to sell us books

00:06:12.772 --> 00:06:14.840
full of inside dirt
about the Trump White House.

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.109
The latest attempt comes from
a guy named Cliff Sims,

00:06:17.109 --> 00:06:18.377
who worked in
the White House

00:06:18.377 --> 00:06:19.945
as Trump's director
of message strategy.

00:06:19.945 --> 00:06:21.280
His new book
about the White House

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.748
is called
"Team of Vipers."

00:06:22.748 --> 00:06:24.650
In the books,
Sims reveals details

00:06:24.650 --> 00:06:26.452
of Trump's interactions
with other Republicans,

00:06:26.452 --> 00:06:28.454
like former House Speaker
Paul Ryan.

00:06:28.454 --> 00:06:30.489
Sims relays a story
about what happened

00:06:30.489 --> 00:06:32.925
the rare time Ryan said
he disagreed with Trump.

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.960
Trump called up Ryan,
and yelled at him.

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:37.096
-The book also goes on
to describe the president

00:06:37.096 --> 00:06:39.999
reacting to Ryan
distancing himself from Trump

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:42.167
in October 2016,

00:06:42.167 --> 00:06:44.670
in the aftermath of
the Access Hollywood tape.

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:47.006
Quote, "I remember
being in Wisconsin,

00:06:47.006 --> 00:06:50.376
and your own people were booing
you," Trump told Ryan.

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:54.313
"You were out there dying
like a dog, Paul -- like a dog."

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:57.383
-What does Trump have
against dogs?

00:06:57.383 --> 00:06:59.718
He's always attacking people
by saying they were

00:06:59.718 --> 00:07:02.288
"fired like dog,"
or "choked like a dog,"

00:07:02.288 --> 00:07:04.457
or they were
"begging for money like a dog,"

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:08.260
or they got "kicked out of
the ABC News debate like a dog."

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:09.962
Dogs don't...

00:07:09.962 --> 00:07:11.864
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:11.864 --> 00:07:14.800
Dogs don't do
any of those things.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:18.738
And if a dog got up on a stage
at a debate with you,

00:07:18.738 --> 00:07:22.475
not only would it not get booed,
it would probably get elected.

00:07:22.475 --> 00:07:24.576
[ Laughter ]

00:07:24.576 --> 00:07:27.346
But here's the thing --
Sims still says he was proud

00:07:27.346 --> 00:07:29.848
to work for Trump. In fact,
he went so far as to say

00:07:29.848 --> 00:07:32.885
that Trump doesn't have
a racist bone in his body.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:34.920
If that's the case,
it's because he doesn't have

00:07:34.920 --> 00:07:36.455
any bones in his body
at all.

00:07:36.455 --> 00:07:37.756
I mean, look at him.

00:07:37.756 --> 00:07:40.359
I didn't think it was possible
for someone to look like

00:07:40.359 --> 00:07:42.595
a sad version of
the Kool-Aid man.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:43.863
[ Laughter ]

00:07:43.863 --> 00:07:46.632
"Oh...no.

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.867
Oh, no.

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:50.903
Sorry about you wall."

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:54.206
[ Laughter ]

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:56.409
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:59.311 --> 00:08:01.013
So, in an interview with
the New York this week,

00:08:01.013 --> 00:08:02.715
staff writer
Isaac Chotiner

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:04.316
asked Sims
a very simple question

00:08:04.316 --> 00:08:06.118
about Trump's
racist crusade

00:08:06.118 --> 00:08:08.320
to prove that Barack Obama
was not born in America.

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.422
But Sims didn't want to answer,
because he knew it would

00:08:10.422 --> 00:08:12.324
contradict his claim
that Trump isn't a racist.

00:08:12.324 --> 00:08:15.260
So, the resulting conversation
went in circles forever.

00:08:15.260 --> 00:08:16.629
Here are some highlights.

00:08:16.629 --> 00:08:18.597
"What's your understanding
or birtherism?"

00:08:18.597 --> 00:08:19.998
"What do you mean?

00:08:19.998 --> 00:08:22.167
Like, what do you mean,
what's my understanding of it?"

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:24.136
"What the president
was doing there."

00:08:24.136 --> 00:08:26.772
"I have no idea."
"Oh."

00:08:26.772 --> 00:08:29.108
"I don't really know
what that was all about."

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:31.477
"You are selling yourself
as a smart D.C. insider,

00:08:31.477 --> 00:08:33.312
and yet, you are telling me
here, on the record,

00:08:33.312 --> 00:08:35.047
that you have no idea
what that was about?

00:08:35.047 --> 00:08:36.983
Is that really
what you are doing?"

00:08:36.983 --> 00:08:38.951
"I know what it was about."

00:08:38.951 --> 00:08:40.919
"So, what do you think
it was about?"

00:08:40.919 --> 00:08:42.521
"I don't know."

00:08:42.521 --> 00:08:44.556
"Really?
You don't know?"

00:08:44.556 --> 00:08:47.092
"I guess I'm confused
at what you were asking."

00:08:47.092 --> 00:08:49.295
"You keep saying you know
what birtherism is about,

00:08:49.295 --> 00:08:51.430
but you are not telling me
what you think it was about.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:53.265
So, what do you think
it is about?"

00:08:53.265 --> 00:08:55.400
"So, I think that's, like,
a great example of time

00:08:55.400 --> 00:08:56.802
where he does not
step up to the plate

00:08:56.802 --> 00:08:59.071
and take on these race issues
in an appropriate way,

00:08:59.071 --> 00:09:00.606
a helpful way,
for the country.

00:09:00.606 --> 00:09:02.641
No doubt that
that was terrible.

00:09:02.641 --> 00:09:04.543
I don't know what else
you want me to say about it."

00:09:04.543 --> 00:09:06.578
"We have been talking
for five minutes about this,

00:09:06.578 --> 00:09:09.314
and it took you that long
to say that?

00:09:09.314 --> 00:09:11.316
I mean, geez, I've heard
people more comfortable

00:09:11.316 --> 00:09:14.553
getting a full cavity search
at the airport.

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:15.754
What do you mean,

00:09:15.754 --> 00:09:16.822
you're not following
the line of questioning?

00:09:16.822 --> 00:09:18.624
The question was,
'What is birtherism?'

00:09:18.624 --> 00:09:21.260
Were your high-school essays
this bad?"

00:09:21.260 --> 00:09:22.995
[ Laughter ]

00:09:22.995 --> 00:09:24.730
Trump is the most famous
grifter in politics.

00:09:24.730 --> 00:09:26.798
But like all grifters,
he attracts other grifters.

00:09:26.798 --> 00:09:29.734
They're just as complicit
in his agenda as anyone else,

00:09:29.734 --> 00:09:30.903
even though he's an...

00:09:30.903 --> 00:09:34.840
-"Egotistical,
billionaire [bleep]."

00:09:34.840 --> 00:09:36.375
This has been
"A Closer Look."

00:09:36.375 --> 00:09:40.546
[ Cheers and applause ]

